.TH XD\-USERS 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-users \- User Accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-users
.YS
.SY xd\-users
.B \-\-advanced
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-users
is Windows XP's User Accounts (Control Panel), through AccountsService
.RB ( org.freedesktop.Accounts ).
As in XP, it is a set of task pages: pick a task or an account, then what
to change about it.
.PP
Users change their own name and picture, and their password through
.BR passwd (1),
so the system's password rules apply.
Administrators also change other accounts' names, pictures, passwords and
types, create accounts and delete them; AccountsService asks polkit, so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for an administrator's password.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-advanced
XP's other User Accounts window (\fBcontrol userpasswords2\fR): the users
and "Users must enter a user name and password to use this computer".
Unticked, the user chosen logs on automatically (AccountsService's
automatic logon). Only display managers that read AccountsService's
setting follow it, as GDM does; SDDM and LightDM keep their own, and the
window says which display manager is running.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.face
A copy of the user's picture, which the Start menu shows.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-security (1),
.BR passwd (1)
